#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:2
msgid "nfs-mount interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `nfs-mount` interface allows the mounting and unmounting of Network File "
"System mount points within a snap's writable areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"**Note:** This interface only supports NFSv4. This should not cause problems "
"as earlier versions are now considerably old and are unlikely to be being "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:9
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:11
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`** : "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`** : no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:11
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:14
msgid "Requires snapd version _2.62+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"This interface requires only the addition of `nfs-mount` to a snap's list of "
"`plugs` , unlike other mounting interfaces which require additional rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:18
msgid ""
"Additionally, the userspace binaries required to mount shares are not "
"included in base snaps. They will need to be installed manually from the "
"`nfs-common` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:20
msgid "<h3 id='heading-code'>Code examples</h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"The following is a simple example `snapcraft.yaml` with accompanying _mount_ "
"and _unmount_ scripts for a snap that will mount and unmount an NFS share "
"within `$SNAP_COMMON`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:24
msgid ""
"name: nfs4-example\n"
"base: core22\n"
"version: '0.1'\n"
"summary: Example Snap showing off the new nfs-mount interface.\n"
"description: |\n"
"  This snap provides two commands: nfs-mount and nfs-unmount.\n"
"  Mount takes a single argument in the form of <hostname>:<nfs-share-name>.\n"
"\n"
"grade: stable\n"
"confinement: strict\n"
"\n"
"apps:\n"
"  nfs-mount:\n"
"    command: bin/nfs-mount.sh\n"
"    plugs: [nfs-mount]\n"
"  nfs-unmount:\n"
"    command: bin/nfs-unmount.sh\n"
"    plugs: [nfs-mount]\n"
"\n"
"parts:\n"
"  scripts:\n"
"    plugin: dump\n"
"    source: ./src\n"
"    organize:\n"
"      '*': bin/\n"
"  packages:\n"
"    plugin: nil\n"
"    stage-packages: [nfs-common]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:55
msgid "The mount script `nfs-mount.sh`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:56
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh -eux\n"
"\n"
"# If not argument is provided, print help and exit\n"
"[ -n \"$1\" ] || {\n"
"  printf '%s <hostname>:<nfs-share-path>\\n' \"$0\"\n"
"  exit 1\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"# Ensure that the mount point has been created\n"
"[ -d \"${SNAP_COMMON}/mnt\" ] \\\n"
"  || mkdir -p \"${SNAP_COMMON}/mnt\"\n"
"\n"
"# Attempt to mount the share\n"
"mount.nfs4 \"$1\" \"${SNAP_COMMON}/mnt\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:73
msgid "And the unmount script, `nfs-unmount.sh`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/nfs-mount-interface.md:75
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh -eux\n"
"\n"
"umount \"${SNAP_COMMON}/mnt\"\n"
msgstr ""

